		{"id":"616b372124b7f034","type":"group","x":4680,"y":-689,"width":480,"height":4209,"color":"2","label":"Prehopsital Treatment"},
		{"id":"94b7c0c6d9af5002","type":"group","x":1500,"y":840,"width":900,"height":1314},
		{"id":"ec5848c9ffc6d4f8","type":"group","x":-271,"y":244,"width":758,"height":1011,"color":"3","label":"Hx"},
		{"id":"07f26fd7ef63860f","type":"group","x":1500,"y":-580,"width":900,"height":734},
		{"id":"d415ffdf77de0bb8","type":"group","x":1500,"y":196,"width":900,"height":595},
		{"id":"8044b450098e5588","type":"group","x":1562,"y":3600,"width":916,"height":520},
		{"id":"7fc61ecfc66c6833","type":"group","x":1562,"y":3000,"width":889,"height":501},
		{"id":"b7e5937d38a958a4","type":"group","x":3356,"y":2409,"width":234,"height":381,"color":"#b3ad00"},
		{"id":"fbc9819b5931bce0","type":"group","x":3055,"y":2409,"width":234,"height":323,"color":"#b3ad00"},
		{"id":"c617acbb56db7ba7","type":"group","x":2736,"y":2187,"width":118,"height":247,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"3aea6950783831c7","type":"text","text":"### **Nausea / Vomiting**\n- Onset, timing after meals\n- Vomit description:\n    - Fresh blood (MW tear / varices)\n    - Coffee ground (ulcer)\n    - Undigested food (stricture / pouch / achalasia)\n    - Non-bilious (pyloric obstruction)\n    - Bilious/faecal (lower GI obstruction)","x":1890,"y":957,"width":407,"height":304,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"4714ca9a7cafc4de","type":"text","text":"### **Symptoms**\n- SOB (rest / exertion, worsening)\n- Wheeze\n- Cough (onset, progression, type: clear / yellow / green / brown / bloody)\n- Cough timing (meals, seasonal, around others)\n- Associated: breathlessness / chest pain / runny nose\n- Snoring / apnoea at night\n- Recent travel / immobility","x":1868,"y":303,"width":429,"height":320},
		{"id":"263813d2c4eb9f8c","type":"text","text":"### [[Review of the Eyes, Ears, Nose and Throat]]","x":1555,"y":2180,"width":520,"height":50,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"1a032a65a8a9ec99","type":"text","text":"### **Other**\n- Pain (intermittent/constant, meal-related, posture-related)\n- Abdominal bloating / distension","x":2124,"y":1339,"width":258,"height":222,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"82a61fc5a5d58bad","type":"text","text":"### **Bowels**\n- Normal habits?\n- Constipation / diarrhoea / urgency / incontinence\n- Stool change (loose, hard, black, red, fatty)\n- Passing wind?\n- Straining?","x":1800,"y":1303,"width":275,"height":285,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"d45e2ec6c35ba859","type":"text","text":"## EENT Constellation\n\n- Ear: Pain, discharge, decreased hearing, tinnitus, dizziness, balance problems\n- Nose: Congestion, runny nose, nosebleeds, sinus pressure\n- Throat: Sore throat, difficulty swallowing, hoarseness, chronic cough    \n- Eyes: Blurred vision, eye pain, redness, double vision, floaters, itching, excessive tearing, light sensitivity","x":777,"y":1642,"width":415,"height":334,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"358bf200fde050f0","type":"text","text":"## GIT Constellation\n- Abdominal pain and cramping\n- Bloating, gas\n- Nausea, vomiting\n- Heartburn, indigestion\n- Diarrhea or constipation\n- Blood in stool (red or black)\n- Change in bowel habits","x":777,"y":1038,"width":415,"height":334,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"a8823e0f4c2f1df5","type":"text","text":"### [[Questions for Gastrointestinal Exam]]","x":1735,"y":862,"width":424,"height":50,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"78bf888975b88836","type":"text","text":"### **History**\n- GI disease / surgery / CVD (adhesions, mesenteric ischemia)\n- Alcohol use\n- Medications (antibiotics, steroids, opioids)\n- Pregnancy","x":1520,"y":940,"width":324,"height":241,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"2a62884caca942e7","type":"text","text":"### **Diet / Eating**\n- Swallowing difficulty\n- Heartburn / indigestion\n- Diet/appetite changes\n- Unintentional weight loss","x":1520,"y":1232,"width":256,"height":213,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"7399c387c96c4b44","type":"text","text":"### **History**\n- Diagnosed GU disease?\n- Past STDs?","x":1591,"y":1712,"width":224,"height":151,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"6bc38e3ce137863f","type":"text","text":"### **Other**\n- Genital discharge","x":1606,"y":1957,"width":238,"height":94,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"1428a0a4fa09f2ad","type":"text","text":"### [[Review of the Genito-urinary System]]","x":1714,"y":1617,"width":465,"height":50,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a76652ea4ec4f042","type":"text","text":"### **Urinary Symptoms**\n- Fluid intake normal?\n- Urine: volume, colour, odour (dark = red flag)\n- Dysuria / burning / pain\n- Flank pain or tenderness\n- Urine stream: weak, delayed start, dribble at end\n- Nocturia (getting up at night)\n- Polyuria (passing more than normal)","x":1971,"y":1712,"width":349,"height":339,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"93037ba0a92c1ff3","type":"text","text":"### Are you in any pain?","x":-222,"y":543,"width":250,"height":102,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"b38567599db9a2a9","type":"text","text":"## Biopsychosocial Hx\n'PASTSOFS' - \n- Psych\n- [[Checklist - ADLs]]\n- Social\n- Travel\n- Surgical\n- Occupational\n- Family\n- Sexual","x":-251,"y":874,"width":309,"height":360,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"703a2c5a3ea3396b","type":"text","text":"### Summarise Initial Findings and Identify Relevant Constellation(s)","x":313,"y":1454,"width":309,"height":120,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"cd6eb18617519657","type":"text","text":"### [[Vital Sign Survey (VSS)]]\n- HR\n- BP\n- RR\n- SpO2\n- BGL\n- GCS\n- Temp\n- ECG 12-Lead","x":-97,"y":1468,"width":250,"height":344},
		{"id":"17182ba88c8784c5","type":"text","text":"## Gait, Arms, Legs, and Spine\n\n- Abnormal gait (limping, shuffling, unsteady, wide-based, dragging toes, foot drop, festinating)\n- Difficulty with coordination and balance\n- Muscle weakness or stiffness\n- Radiating pain (from spine to arms or legs)\n- Numbness, tingling, or altered sensation","x":777,"y":2129,"width":415,"height":280,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"f74a6f91f6a794fd","type":"text","text":"## Neurological (Upper and Lower)\n- Weakness (general or focal)\n- Muscle spasms or cramps\n- Sensory changes (numbness, tingling)\n- Poor coordination or loss of fine motor skills\n- Difficulty speaking or swallowing\n- Seizures, tremors, altered consciousness\n- Mental/cognitive changes (confusion, memory loss, mood changes)","x":777,"y":2560,"width":415,"height":360,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"bea48215406b951a","type":"text","text":"## Respiratory Constellation\n- Cough (dry or productive)\n- Shortness of breath\n- Wheezing\n- Chest tightness or pain\n- Sore throat\n- Runny or stuffy nose\n- Fever, chills\n- Fatigue and weakness","x":777,"y":435,"width":415,"height":334,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"f8a316ed94de04b0","type":"text","text":"## Cardiovascular Constellation\n\n- Chest pain or discomfort\n- Palpitations (racing or irregular heartbeats)\n- SOB\n- Fatigue\n- Swelling in legs, ankles, or feet\n- Syncope\n- Pain radiating to arms, jaw, or back","x":777,"y":-129,"width":415,"height":334,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"101240b3903c9197","type":"text","text":"## Cranial Nerves\n- Visual changes (double vision, visual field loss)\n- Facial numbness or weakness, drooping\n- Hearing loss, tinnitus\n- Changes in taste or smell\n- Difficulty swallowing, chewing, or speaking (dysarthria/dysphagia)\n- Abnormal eye movements, drooping eyelid (ptosis)\n- Loss of balance or dizziness","x":777,"y":3050,"width":415,"height":360,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"a38bb0c28d806d6c","type":"text","text":"## Community Paramedicine OSCE","x":-340,"y":-216,"width":486,"height":60},
		{"id":"caeee5c80a02a3fb","type":"text","text":"### OPQRST\n- When did it start?\n- Better or Worse?\n- Describe the pain?\n- Does it move anywhere ?\n- x/10?\n- How long and when?","x":173,"y":509,"width":294,"height":272,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"16dac2e2b07edf34","type":"text","text":"## Introduce Self + INFORMED CONSENT","x":-366,"y":60,"width":539,"height":80,"color":"1"},
