			"type":"text",
			"text":"**IX & X Glossopharyngeal and Vagus Nerve** \n\n- Assess swallowing\n- Observe uvula and soft palate for movement\n- Listen to quality of speech",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":3358,
			"y":3523,
			"width":261,
			"height":201,
			"color":"6"
		},
		{
			"id":"f3236d85b1b55721",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**Sensation**",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":3076,
			"y":3229,
			"width":132,
			"height":60,
			"color":"#00ff40"
		},
		{
			"id":"52d6c7180e8b2d19",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**V Trigeminal Nerve** \n- facial sensation (soft, spikey)\n- jaw movement \n",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":3080,
			"y":3523,
			"width":187,
			"height":137,
			"color":"6"
		},
		{
			"id":"779c50712f9945c2",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"### [[Cranial Nerves, Examination]]",
			"styleAttributes":{"shape":"parallelogram"},
			"x":2994,
			"y":3421,
			"width":360,
			"height":60,
			"color":"6"
		},
		{
			"id":"e21a47386fcc0648",
			"type":"text",
			"text":" **II Optic Nerve**\n [[Test visual acuity]]\n [[Assess visual fields]]",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":2753,
			"y":3633,
			"width":197,
			"height":119,
			"color":"6"
		},
		{
			"id":"2963f714f2f56eeb",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"1. **T**witchy **P**eople **R**eally **S**care **C**ats.",
			"styleAttributes":{"shape":"pill"},
			"x":2760,
			"y":3319,
			"width":324,
			"height":76,
			"color":"#00ff40"
		},
		{"id":"cc13b48d9a47bbf3","type":"text","text":"### **History**\n- Diagnosed neurological conditions?\n- Stroke or head injury?\n","x":1609,"y":3740,"width":284,"height":162},
		{"id":"0ffd095a07f6959c","type":"text","text":"### [[Review of the Neurological System]]","x":1582,"y":3620,"width":338,"height":80,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"013788a8be301fb0","type":"text","text":"### **Symptoms**\n- Fits / faints / “funny turns”\n- Weakness, numbness, clumsiness, balance problems\n- Sensory issues: vision, hearing, smell, balance\n- Headaches:\n    - Sudden/severe → subarachnoid haemorrhage\n    - Fever/chills/neck stiffness → meningitis/encephalitis\n    - Increasing frequency/intensity → space-occupying lesion\n    - With focal signs → CVA or lesion\n    - Temporal tenderness → temporal arteritis\n- Recent trauma → haemorrhage risk\n- Sleep difficulties\n- Mood: sadness, depression, anxiety (“nerves”)\n- Memory changes","x":1942,"y":3620,"width":516,"height":480},
		{"id":"a60de4f630b41aec","type":"text","text":"### [[Review of the Musculoskeletal System]]","x":1589,"y":3050,"width":480,"height":50,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"41940cc42bf1eb71","type":"text","text":"### **Symptoms**\n- Joint pain / stiffness\n- Joint redness / swelling\n- Back or neck pain (acute vs chronic)\n    - Red flags: cancer history, fever/chills/weight loss, sensory loss (legs/groin), bladder/bowel change, persistent >4wks, not relieved\n- Rash (dermatomyositis)\n- Fingers painful/white/blue in cold (Raynaud’s)\n- Function: button shirt, climb stairs, hang washing (ADLs)","x":2106,"y":3020,"width":320,"height":461},
		{"id":"cab3a4f986e256cc","type":"text","text":"### **History**\n- MSK condition diagnosed?\n- Rheumatoid arthritis or gout?\n","x":1629,"y":3161,"width":244,"height":180},
		{
			"id":"9a14ea9b8cd98d6f",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**VII Facial Nerve**\n-  taste \n- Assess facial muscle movements",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":3057,
			"y":3705,
			"width":234,
			"height":141,
			"color":"6"
		},
		{
			"id":"ce7260bd8321fcda",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**VIII Vestibulocochlear Nerve** \n-  hearing assessment Webbers, Rhines\n- Perform Romberg's test (for balance)",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":3040,
			"y":3909,
			"width":251,
			"height":176,
			"color":"6"
		},
		{
			"id":"8604c0467c03acb2",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"[[Modified-modified Schober’s test]]",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":2787,
			"y":2667,
			"width":142,
			"height":115,
			"color":"#b3ad00"
		},
		{"id":"1e1308dc346f0956","type":"text","text":"### Upper Limb?","x":2503,"y":2706,"width":136,"height":69},
		{
			"id":"3876424097c7f151",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**Coordination**\n- Finger-to-nose test\n",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":3398,
			"y":2993,
			"width":174,
			"height":96,
			"color":"#00ff40"
		},
		{
			"id":"90f206c5bd2301e9",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"### [[Neurological, Upper limb Examination]]",
			"styleAttributes":{"shape":"parallelogram"},
			"x":2934,
			"y":2888,
			"width":480,
			"height":50,
			"color":"2"
		},
		{
			"id":"6b6505cbe7c10551",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**Reflexes**\n- Biceps\n- Supinator (brachioradialis)\n- Triceps\n- Assess bilaterally",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":3044,
			"y":2965,
			"width":196,
			"height":195,
			"color":"#00ff40"
		},
		{
			"id":"72b561438664fe62",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**History and General**\n\n\n\n\n\n",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":2787,
			"y":2935,
			"width":123,
			"height":60,
			"color":"2"
		},
		{"id":"d93579269fd01564","type":"text","text":"### Throat\n- **Throat / Larynx** → pain\n- difficulty swallowing?\n- hoarseness, voice changes?\n- Lung sounds? Breath sounds? → infection, cancer, overuse, injury\n- **Hoarseness** → short-term = laryngitis; persistent = carcinoma, nerve injury\n- **Neck injury** → trauma-related\n- **Smoking** → laryngeal / lung cancer, recurrent nerve palsy\n- **Steroid inhaler / voice use / recent intubation** → overuse, papilloma, injury\n- **Thyroid disease** → hypothyroidism affecting voice\n- **Oral pain** → toothache, TMJ, angina\n- **Painful swallowing** → tonsillitis, ulcers\n- **Duration** → acute = infection\n- **Dental problems** → source of mouth/throat pain","x":1215,"y":2616,"width":681,"height":440},
		{"id":"b3aac5cfdb1ac543","type":"text","text":"### Ears\n- **Ear** → tinnitus, vertigo, hearing loss, pain, discharge → infection, Ménière’s, trauma\n- **Hearing duration / congenital** → congenital vs acquired\n- **Noise exposure (work / hobbies)** → noise-induced hearing loss\n- **Ototoxic drugs (salicylates, cisplatin, gentamicin)** → drug-induced hearing loss\n- **Family history** → otosclerosis\n- **Recurrent ear infections** → chronic infection risk\n- **Wax, trauma, meningitis history** → structural or infection-related hearing problems\n- **Ringing in ears** → Ménière’s disease","x":1915,"y":2616,"width":550,"height":350},
		{"id":"c504e2f4032c6506","type":"text","text":"## **General**\n- **Fever / chills / weight changes** ?\n- **Trachea** → noisy/difficulty breathing → obstruction\n- **Neck** → lymphadenopathy, lumps, swelling → infection, malignancy\n- **Face / sinuses** → pain, swelling, numbness → sinusitis, infection, nerve involvement","x":1306,"y":2123,"width":419,"height":275},
		{"id":"7ae1f32e69c7fbe2","type":"text","text":"### Nose\n- **Nose** → congestion, runny nose, nosebleeds, decreased smell → infection, allergy, polyps\n- - **Duration / laterality** → acute infection vs septal deviation\n- **Allergies / polyps / seasonality / sneezing** → allergic rhinitis\n- **Injury / foreign body** → trauma, obstruction\n- **Other symptoms** → loss of smell (polyps), headache/fullness (sinusitis), fever","x":1751,"y":2123,"width":483,"height":335},
		{"id":"69cae6ab58624fd6","type":"text","text":"- Persistent with one eye closed → visual field defect\n    - Curtain over vision → amaurosis fugax\n    - Previous strokes / heart issues → retinal embolus / cortical infarct\n    - Eye pain → acute glaucoma, iritis\n    - Trauma → optic nerve/eye injury\n    - Preceding flashing lights → migraine\n    - Severe ipsilateral headache → temporal arteritis\n    - Weakness / tingling / bladder-bowel issues → MS / optic neuritis\n    - Diabetes → diabetic retinopathy","x":2168,"y":2228,"width":490,"height":341},
		{"id":"95845044fcf6d76f","type":"text","text":"## Eyes\n- **Contact lenses** → risk of corneal ulceration\n- **Pain with eye movement** → iritis, scleritis\n- **Lids stuck together in morning** → conjunctivitis\n- **Eye injuries / exposure (dust, metal, welding)** → trauma, foreign body, flash burn\n- **Arthritis or rashes** → systemic vasculitis affecting eyes\n- **Sudden visual loss**?\n","x":1306,"y":2419,"width":475,"height":331}
	],
	"edges":[
